NOTE: results above are from the corrected MultiStreamDataset (n_context-aware
target restriction). An earlier uncorrected run (discarded) allowed seq_len<30
windows to target dates inside the 30-day context copied from the preceding
split, which could contaminate validation with disguised training targets, and
also under-counted available windows inconsistently across window lengths.
The corrected run above ensures seq_len in {7,14,21,30} all evaluate on the
FULL 547 val targets (fair comparison), while seq_len in {45,60} correctly
evaluate on fewer targets (532/517) since the 30-day context cannot cover
lookback windows longer than 30 days - this is reported honestly rather than
hidden.

SELECTED WINDOW: seq_len=21 (lowest val loss among all 6 candidates, and among
the 4 candidates {7,14,21,30} evaluated on the identical, full 547-window val
set). This is also consistent with the empirically measured ~14-21 day
revenue-to-cash-collection lag structure found during the EDA audit (peak
correlation between TOTAL_GROSS_CHARGES and CASH_COLLECTED at lag=14 days;
autocorrelation of both targets drops sharply between lag 21 and lag 30 -
see final report "Upgrade 8" section).
